---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/site';
const breadcrumbs = breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about' }], Astro.site ?? SITE_URL);
---

<Base title="About · Hotlines" description="How the World Emergency & Hotlines directory works: data sourcing, verification, routing, and privacy." jsonLd={breadcrumbs}>
  <article class="prose prose-invert mx-auto max-w-2xl text-fg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.title">About this project</h1>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      World Emergency & Hotlines is a public directory of listed crisis, emergency, and support services
      across countries and territories. Coverage, source information, and verification status vary and are shown per record. We think nobody should have to search in a panic.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.crisisTitle">If you're in crisis right now</h2>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-danger/40 bg-danger/10 p-4 not-prose mb-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-fg-muted">
        Call your country's emergency number. In most of Europe: <span class="font-mono text-fg">112</span>.
        US/Canada: <span class="font-mono text-fg">911</span>. UK: <span class="font-mono text-fg">999</span>.
        Australia: <span class="font-mono text-fg">000</span>. Emergency numbers and access without a SIM vary by country, device, carrier, and network; verify local guidance.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
        For crisis support: <a href="/category/suicide_crisis" class="text-accent hover:underline">find a crisis line →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.useTitle">How to use this site</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Search</strong> by country, category, or service name (e.g. "Italy domestic violence",
        "UK childline", "Canada veterans").
        Use the filter chips to narrow to verified-only, SMS-accessible, or online-chat services.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Browse by category</strong> — see <a href="/categories" class="text-accent hover:underline">all 29 categories</a>
        with counts and verification coverage.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Explore the map</strong> — click any country to see all local numbers and crisis lines.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Country pages</strong> show hotlines grouped by category, with a prioritized listing
        panel at the top and a traveller note about international dialling.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.verificationTitle">How verification works</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Every hotline record carries a verification status. It describes the evidence checked for this directory,
      not whether a line was test-called, answered, or available in real time.
    </p>
    <dl class="space-y-3 not-prose mt-4">
      {[
        ['verified_web',       'bg-success/15 text-success border-success/40',  'The listed details appeared on the organisation\'s official website when checked. This is not a live availability check.'],
        ['verified_authority', 'bg-success/15 text-success border-success/40',  'The listed details appeared in an authoritative source such as a government body when checked.'],
        ['verified_knowledge', 'bg-success/10 text-success border-success/30',  'Checked against a trusted reference source, but not necessarily the provider\'s own page.'],
        ['cross_referenced',   'bg-accent/15 text-accent border-accent/40',     'Found in multiple independent sources but not yet confirmed against the provider or responsible authority.'],
        ['legacy_unverified',  'bg-fg-muted/15 text-fg-muted border-fg-muted/30', 'From an earlier dataset. Has not been independently confirmed. Please check the organisation\'s official website before relying on this number.'],
        ['disputed',           'bg-danger/15 text-danger border-danger/40',     'Conflicting information found. Treat with caution — the number may be wrong.'],
        ['deprecated',         'bg-fg-muted/15 text-fg-muted border-fg-muted/30', 'Believed to be no longer active. Included for reference.'],
      ].map(([status, tone, desc]) => (
        <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class={`chip shrink-0 border text-[11px] mt-0.5 ${tone}`}>{(status as string).replace(/_/g, ' ')}</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-fg-muted">{desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg">Coverage and checked dates</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      A country can have national coverage while still lacking a verified local or specialist option. City, county,
      state/province, national, and global service areas are shown separately where the source supports them. A
      “source checked” date records when the cited page supported the listed details; it does not promise current
      opening hours, wait time, eligibility, or that the service answered a test contact.
    </p>
    <p class="text-fg-muted mt-2">
      If a local option is unavailable, the directory may show a broader regional or national fallback. Report
      disconnected numbers, changed hours, scope errors, closures, or other concerns from the relevant service card.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.routingTitle">Prioritized routing</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      On each country page, the site selects the first source-checked or cross-referenced listing in this category
      order: suicide crisis, mental health, domestic violence, sexual violence, child protection, then general support.
      If none matches, it selects the first listing in the same category order, then the first dataset listing.
    </p>
    <p class="text-fg-muted mt-2">
      This deterministic ordering does not determine suitability, eligibility, live availability, or provide medical
      advice. Search uses separate deterministic scoring; filter chips can restrict results to source-checked or
      channel-specific services.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.travellersTitle">Travellers & expats</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Most freephone/toll-free numbers require a local SIM or network connection for the country. If you're abroad:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-fg-muted">
      <li>Use the relevant <a class="text-accent underline" href="/countries">country page</a> and verify the local emergency number and carrier or SIM requirements.</li>
      <li>Look for hotlines with online chat (💬) — these work internationally over Wi-Fi.</li>
      <li>SMS-based lines (📱) may also work internationally depending on your roaming plan.</li>
      <li>Local authorities or accommodation staff may be able to suggest current contacts, but verify any details they provide.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.privacyTitle">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      The search runs entirely in your browser — your search terms and results never leave your device.
      No queries are logged. The emergency banner reads your browser language setting only (no server call, no location).
      We don't use tracking cookies or analytics that identify individuals.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg">Maintainer and editorial responsibility</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">This directory is maintained through the public <a class="text-accent underline" href="https://github.com/craigrallen/world-emergency-hotlines" rel="noopener" target="_blank">craigrallen/world-emergency-hotlines GitHub project</a>. Maintainers review cited evidence and proposed changes; inclusion does not imply affiliation, endorsement, or a provider relationship. Reviews occur as maintainers process contributions and corrections, without a promised publication cadence.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-fg-muted">To correct or remove a listing, use the correction form linked below and include a public source when possible. Reports of disconnected numbers, changed scope, or safety concerns can also be filed as GitHub issues. Maintainers may amend, dispute, deprecate, or remove a record after reviewing the available evidence.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-fg" data-i18n="about.openDataTitle">Public data access & contributing</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      The dataset is publicly accessible from the <a href="/data" class="text-accent hover:underline">data page</a>
      in JSON format. The repository currently has no license, so access does not itself grant reuse rights. Public submissions are review leads, not verified records, and publication is not guaranteed.
    </p>
    <div class="not-prose mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/data" class="btn-primary">Data downloads →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/craigrallen/world-emergency-hotlines/issues/new?template=hotline-correction.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-ghost">Correct a listing ↗</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/craigrallen/world-emergency-hotlines/issues/new?template=provider-submission.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-ghost">Submit a provider ↗</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
